ted-in-irregular-warfare-initiative-piece-on-us-influence-in-the-global-economy/'}, {'signal_id': 'a93318277703c060', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Russia Sanctions Database cited in Forbes article on the war in Ukraine <p>Read the article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/russia-sanctions-database-cited-in-forbes-article-on-the-war-in-ukraine/">Russia Sanctions Database', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/russia-sanctions-database-cited-in-forbes-article-on-the-war-in-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': 'eaacdd903578df5a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lipsky quoted in Semafor article on China’s efforts to dethrone the dollar <p>Read the article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-semafor-article-on-chinas-efforts-to-dethrone-the-dollar/">Lipsky quoted in Sem', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-semafor-article-on-chinas-efforts-to-dethrone-the-dollar/'}, {'signal_id': '084096876f847ee8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'De Kruijf cited in Standard Chartered report on Islamic Finance <p>Read the full report here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/de-kruijf-cited-in-standard-chartered-report-on-islamic-finance/">De Kruijf cited in Standard Chartered', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/de-kruijf-cited-in-standard-chartered-report-on-islamic-finance/'}, {'signal_id': '0358957b06236b18', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'AC Front Page event with Federal Reserve Vice Chair Michelle Bowman covered by The Wall Street Journal in an article on the Fed’s outlook for further rate increases <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/l', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-the-prospects-of-de-dollarization-4/'}, {'signal_id': '6bed131a07b15168', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'AC Front Page event with Federal Reserve Vice Chair Michelle Bowman covered by American Banker in an article on eSLR reform and Treasury market functioning <p>Watch the full interview here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/goldsmi', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/goldsmith-romero-interviewed-on-cnn-about-the-rise-in-prediction-market-trading-2/'}, {'signal_id': '838d5977355a4251', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'AC Front Page event with Federal Reserve Vice Chair Michelle Bowman featured on C-SPAN in coverage of her remarks on financial regulation modernization <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quot', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-6/'}, {'signal_id': '2127b9ace04aab37', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'AC Front Page with Federal Reserve Vice Chair Michelle Bowman featured in Seeking Alpha article on eSLR reform and market liquidity <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-t', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-5/'}, {'signal_id': 'a2553d4d3bb19d98', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'AC Front Page event with Federal Reserve Vice Chair Michelle Bowman featured in a Bloomberg video on the outlook for Fed rate moves <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/our-event-with-the-imfs-christian-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/our-event-with-the-imfs-christian-mumssen-was-written-about-in-a-reuters-article-2/'}, {'signal_id': 'aad57d1ed6f4b3d0', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lipsky quoted in France 24 article on G20 trade talks and the impact of Trump’s tariffs <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-doll', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4/'}, {'signal_id': '91b460ea962e0dd5', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'CBDC Tracker cited in Citi report, The Connective Tissue of Digital Finance: Interoperability, Programmability, and the Path to Institutional Scale. <p>Read the article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited-in-coindesk-on-the-number-of-countries-actively-testing-or-developing-cbdcs-2/'}, {'signal_id': 'f753bcda01e1ee02', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chhangani cited in Forbes article on Saudi Arabia’s withdrawal from the mBridge CBDC platform. <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-3/'}, {'signal_id': 'd68ead9a82c828af', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'De Kruijf cited in National Interest article on the Trump administration’s policy toward the International Criminal Court (ICC) <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-bloomberg-article-o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-bloomberg-article-on-the-impact-of-usmca-uncertainty-on-supply-chains-2/'}, {'signal_id': '815479d013ed2eca', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Trump will define his legacy through Russia—one way or the other <p>The US president inherited Russia’s war on Ukraine, but he will own the consequences of how it ends.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/trump-will-define-his', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/trump-will-define-his-legacy-through-russia-one-way-or-the-other/'}, {'signal_id': '7c96f28b319b0b20', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukrainians are not fighting for Zelenskyy. They are fighting for national survival. <p>Trump and Putin both seem to think that removing Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy would set the stage for a Kremlin-friendly peace deal, but most Ukrainians see the war as a fight for na', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukrainians-are-not-fighting-for-zelenskyy-they-are-fighting-for-survival/'}, {'signal_id': 'e1aa97b5e500a1d3', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The new Middle East is modular <p>In the Middle East today, states are aligning issue by issue, not choosing sides. They cooperate in one area and compete in the next. This modular alignment is shaping the region, even as it manages the shocks of war and energy-market volatility.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/the-big-story/the-new-middle-east-is-modular/'}, {'signal_id': '031868c41e60b35a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in The Sun on potential attacks on undersea infrastructure <p>On October 17, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed in The Sun to discuss the threat of attacks on undersea cables and pipelines.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/braw-in-the-sun-on', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/braw-in-the-sun-on-potential-attacks-on-undersea-infrastructure/'}, {'signal_id': '4c846462d1991272', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The withdrawal of the US-led coalition is a loss for Iraq’s sovereignty <p>The government secured the withdrawal of foreign partners before securing obedience from armed factions. That leaves Baghdad with less leverage against Iran’s allies in Iraq.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/the-withdrawal-of-the-us-led-coalition-is-a-loss-for-iraqs-sovereignty/'}, {'signal_id': 'a4b90adb56fe2f62', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Washington should stop expecting the Gulf to speak with one voice <p>Gulf states are emerging from the Iran war with different conclusions about how to protect themselves and deal with Tehran.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/washington-should-s', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/washington-should-stop-expecting-the-gulf-to-speak-with-one-voice/'}, {'signal_id': 'de76972bfc933bc8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Moldova’s fight against Kremlin interference faces Gagauzia election test <p>Moldova’s democratic resilience faces a revealing litmus test on November 15, when autonomous Gagauzia elects a new governor and People’s Assembly amid concerns over Kremlin interference, write Laurențiu', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/moldovas-fight-against-kremlin-interference-faces-gagauzia-election-test/'}, {'signal_id': 'af88f29163bd1dfa', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Russian attacks on Ukrainian civilians may have a domestic dimension <p>Russia's escalating bombing campaign against civilian targets across Ukraine aims to make much of the country unlivable while also serving a propaganda purpose for the Kremlin on the home front, write Syrus S", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/russian-attacks-on-ukrainian-civilians-may-have-a-domestic-dimension/'}, {'signal_id': 'e15af6013a810c50', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What a Lula or Bolsonaro victory would mean for Brazil and the world <p>Brazil’s presidential runoff could open a narrow window for closer US-Brazil cooperation on trade, security, and critical minerals.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-a-l', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-a-lula-or-bolsonaro-victory-would-mean-for-brazil-and-the-world/'}, {'signal_id': '44541680cfbd5949', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The rewiring of globalization is under way <p>Global supply chains are being reconfigured in response to geopolitical and economic upheaval. This is a more nuanced picture than the term "deglobalization" suggests.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/eco', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/the-rewiring-of-globalization-is-under-way/'}, {'signal_id': 'af04b48c5709ed18', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'After Bosnia’s election, a way forward or deeper deadlock? | A Debrief with Ivana Korajlić <p>Europe Center Resident Senior Fellow Ilva Tare speaks with Ivana Korajlić about Bosnia and Herzegovina\'s October 4 election.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/cont', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/balkans-debrief/after-bosnias-election-a-way-forward-or-deeper-deadlock-a-debrief-with-ivana-korajlic/'}, {'signal_id': '56e53df588937cee', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The European Union as a compound power in Cold War 2.0 <p>Contrary to the prevailing narrative, the European Union has the economic power and strategic vision to act as a credible major power. Willingness to act is the missing piece. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlantic', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/the-european-union-as-a-compound-power-in-cold-war-2-0/'}, {'signal_id': 'c68deb94dd51b676', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Canadian west coast oil as a hedge for East Asian energy security <p>Canadian oil imports can provide insurance and reliability for East Asian countries amid the instability of oil supply from the Middle East.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-rese', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/canadian-west-coast-oil-as-a-hedge-for-east-asian-energy-security/'}, {'signal_id': '0d382bc10d83ae61', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Four ways the midterms can reshape US energy policy <p>The next Congress has options to act, particularly if one or both chambers shift from a Republican to a Democratic majority.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/four-ways-the-midterms-can-resha', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/four-ways-the-midterms-can-reshape-us-energy-policy/'}, {'signal_id': '126f305eab251841', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What Ukraine’s Starlink disruptions reveal about the tradeoffs involved in military commercial dependencies <p>Militaries need to understand the consequences of losing access to capabilities that have become essential to mission execution. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.at', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-ukraines-starlink-disruptions-reveal-about-the-tradeoffs-involved-in-military-commercial-dependencies/'}, {'signal_id': '7fec6ebba9f05f73', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Formula 1 CEO on AI, geopolitics, and leadership <p>Formula 1 (F1) President and CEO Stefano Domenicali discusses the forces shaping the future of F1, from the growing influence of artificial intelligence to the geopolitical challenges of racing around the world. He also reflects', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/inflection-points-with-frederick-kempe/formula-1-ceo-on-ai-geopolitics-and-leadership/'}, {'signal_id': '143c8e612f26090d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw on Bloomberg Television on Trump not ruling out ‘mother of all bombs’ on Iran <p>On October 16, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed on Bloomberg Television to discuss Trump weighing the use of the &#8216;mother of all bombs&#8217; in future Iran air strikes.</p>\n<p>The post <a hr', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-on-bloomberg-television-on-trump-not-ruling-out-mother-of-all-bombs-on-iran/'}, {'signal_id': 'f68c70760905d1b8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Saudi Arabia has more security partners than ever. So why isn’t it safer? <p>Saudi Arabia has succeeded in diversifying its security partnerships. The harder task is turning those wins into security on the ground.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatche', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/saudi-arabia-has-more-security-partners-than-ever-so-why-isnt-it-safer/'}, {'signal_id': '50d2a8ad95180f40', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukrainian drone strikes highlight the vulnerability of Russia’s data centers <p>The idea of Ukrainian drones silencing Kremlin bots clearly caught the world’s imagination, but the real story behind Ukraine’s recent drone strikes on Russia’s mega data centers is one of strategic v', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukrainian-drone-strikes-highlight-the-vulnerability-of-russias-data-centers/'}, {'signal_id': '29dec601b09ce410', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Iraq’s militias are adjusting for a new era, not going away <p>While signaling restraint, the militias are carving room to consolidate their position and shape the terms of Iraq’s next security order.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/iraqs', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/iraqs-militias-are-adjusting-for-a-new-era-not-going-away/'}, {'signal_id': 'f6e80b9d67c9ecbd', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Full transcript: French Finance Minister Roland Lescure on bond market pressure, upcoming elections, and more <p>Lescure appeared at the Atlantic Council studio at the IMF-World Bank Annual Meetings in Bangkok, Thailand.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/co', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/transcript/full-transcript-french-finance-minister-roland-lescure-on-bond-market-pressure-upcoming-elections-and-more/'}, {'signal_id': 'bb844476bf002bc5', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Measuring Europe’s rearmament: A year of the Defence Readiness Roadmap 2030 <p>One year since the EU debuted its "Defence Readiness Roadmap," with forty-five milestones Europe must meet to take responsibility for its own defense by 2030, is the EU on track?</p>\n<p>The post <a hre', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/measuring-europes-rearmament-a-year-of-the-defence-readiness-roadmap-2030/'}, {'signal_id': 'c9c5472a4043430a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Russia’s Starlink substitute poses a security threat far beyond Ukraine <p>The Kremlin is currently in the process of deploying a satellite communications network known as Rassvet, creating concerns for the Russian invasion of Ukraine and for the wider international security envi', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/russias-starlink-substitute-poses-a-security-threat-far-beyond-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': '54175d92aa1627c4', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How torture charges in the Maduro case could close a gap in international justice <p>Congress should seize the moment to add crimes against humanity to a list of crimes that are punishable in the United States even when committed abroad.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlan', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/how-torture-charges-in-the-maduro-case-could-close-a-gap-in-international-justice/'}, {'signal_id': '997fcc7db94ed5e9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukraine reports more battlefield gains as Putin’s invasion loses momentum <p>Kyiv has reported further battlefield gains this week as the country’s Operation Vivaldi counteroffensive in eastern Ukraine’s Donetsk region continues to advance, writes David Kirichenko.</p>\n<p>The pos', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraine-reports-more-battlefield-gains-as-putins-invasion-loses-momentum/'}, {'signal_id': 'a56ff7cf03acab16', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How Syria can avoid the trap of ethno-sectarianism <p>In postwar Iraq and Lebanon, power-sharing agreements allocated top government jobs based on ethnic and religious affiliation. Political deadlock and violence followed. As Syrians rebuild after decades of dictatorship and war,', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/how-syria-can-avoid-the-trap-of-ethno-sectarianism/'}, {'signal_id': 'd44f1dd3ccb49ddb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Toplines: Twenty-five years after anthrax, the US still is not prepared for a biological attack <p>The anthrax events of 2001 transpired twenty-five years ago. The US still needs better preparation against biological attacks.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/toplines-twenty-five-years-after-anthrax-the-us-still-is-not-prepared-for-a-biological-attack/'}, {'signal_id': '6e5269ba88214da9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'ECB President Christine Lagarde on the digital euro and Europe’s financial future <p>As Europe moves closer to a digital euro, European Central Bank President Christine Lagarde discusses the future of Europe’s currency and the importance of payment sovereignty. </p>\n<p>Speaking w', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/podcast/ecb-president-christine-lagarde-on-the-digital-euro-and-europes-financial-future/'}, {'signal_id': '5d5119638fe67cbb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Moldova: How to restore NATO’s deterrence against Russia’s escalating drone attacks <p>Restoring deterrence will require a course correction in the West’s approach to Russia\'s escalating drone attacks.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatc', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dispatch-from-moldova-how-to-restore-natos-deterrence-against-russias-escalating-drone-attacks/'}, {'signal_id': 'c59504cc238174ed', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Tahir in MS NOW on the US Agency for Global Media <p>On October 6, Muhammad Tahir, nonresident senior fellow at the Atlantic Council&#8217;s Eurasia Center, was published in MS NOW on the dangers of reducing the operations of the US Agency for Global Media.</p>\n<p>The post <a hre', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tahir-in-ms-now-on-the-us-agency-for-global-media/'}, {'signal_id': '06aa42e6ccffe795', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from the Gulf: Kuwait still wants Washington but is preparing for less <p>By sheer number of strikes, no country in the Gulf has been hit harder by Iran than the United Arab Emirates. But by exposure and impact, Kuwait may be at the greatest risk.</p>\n<p>The post <a href', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dispatch-from-the-gulf-kuwait-still-wants-washington-but-is-preparing-for-less/'}, {'signal_id': 'f5e04f105e17507e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'When AI agents become economic actors, what happens to money and the financial system? <p>If AI agents come to rely on US transaction infrastructure and dollar-denominated assets, the dollar will become embedded in the operating system of machine commerce. </p>\n<p>The post <a hre', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/geotech-cues/when-ai-agents-become-economic-actors-what-happens-to-money-and-the-financial-system/'}, {'signal_id': '0f7a0af3b1d02db1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Optimizing the NATO 1.5 percent investment commitment for energy security <p>NATO\'s 1.5 percent resilience pledge can be leveraged to build a capability-based energy framework, drawing from lessons in Ukraine and globally.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/optimizing-the-nato-1-5-percent-investment-commitment-for-energy-security/'}, {'signal_id': 'cff6c13f18053457', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ensuring US military readiness in the face of\xa0water, power, and fuel shortages <p>US overseas military installations depend on host nations for power, fuel, and water. A comprehensive review and investment plan is urgently needed to meet the energy and infrastructure security req', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/ensuring-us-military-readiness-in-the-face-of-water-power-and-fuel-shortages/'}, {'signal_id': 'a814656c41c39d8d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Putin snubs Trump’s ceasefire as Russia aims to make Ukraine unlivable <p>Hours after US President Donald Trump’s surprise Sunday announcement of an energy ceasefire between Kyiv and Moscow, Russia responded by bombing a series of Ukrainian power plants, write Maksym Beznosiuk an', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/putin-snubs-trumps-ceasefire-as-russia-aims-to-make-ukraine-unlivable/'}, {'signal_id': 'b71bc1d4b8f96cb3', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How the trade war with Canada is hitting US states—and could sway midterm elections <p>Tariffs on both sides of the border have concentrated the financial burden on specific states and industries, bringing the trade war into some of the country’s most competitive political races.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/how-the-trade-war-with-canada-is-hitting-us-states-and-could-sway-midterm-elections/'}, {'signal_id': '77306b3a1a44d260', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Energy is upending Ukraine peace talks. Our experts explain why. <p>Our experts weighed in on the latest developments, from the "energy ceasefire" announcement to the US-Russia diesel deal.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/energy-ukraine-russia-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/energy-ukraine-russia-diesel-ceasefire/'}, {'signal_id': '848e2dd3c4a4ce64', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Why is electrification no longer “woke”? <p>Once a culture-war issue, electrification is now an AI- and Iran war-era necessity.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/geotech-cues/why-is-electrification-no-longer-woke/">Why is electrification no longer “wo', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/geotech-cues/why-is-electrification-no-longer-woke/'}, {'signal_id': '61a55e31262e5d9a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Live updates from the IMF-World Bank Annual Meetings in Thailand as financial leaders take on AI, debt, and geopolitical upheaval <p>Our experts are on the ground talking to leaders and getting the behind-the-scenes scoop on how the Bretton Woods institutions are taking on the mo', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/live-updates-from-the-imf-world-bank-annual-meetings-in-thailand-as-financial-leaders-take-on-ai-debt-and-geopolitical-upheaval/'}, {'signal_id': 'b981fb9bc5345b69', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in GBNews on Trump’s diesel deal with Russia <p>On October 11, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed on GBNews to discuss US President Donald Trump&#8217;s diesel deal with Russian President Vladimir Putin.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-gbnews-on-trumps-diesel-deal-with-russia/'}, {'signal_id': 'ee9e007d0fee5546', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in New York Post on her new book, “Undersea War” <p>On October 11, Elisabeth Braw was featured in the New York Post in an article discussing her newly released book, &#8220;Undersea War.&#8221;</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-new-y', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-new-york-post-on-her-new-book-undersea-war/'}, {'signal_id': 'd9b67a62ffb6fee8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in DW News on her new book, “Undersea War” <p>On October 10, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed by DW News on her newly released book, &#8220;Undersea War.&#8221;</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/braw-in-dw-news-on-her-new-book-undersea-war/', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/braw-in-dw-news-on-her-new-book-undersea-war/'}, {'signal_id': '0e84098d8032cb32', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The US just sanctioned the International Criminal Court. What’s next? <p>Atlantic Council experts weigh on what Washington\'s sanctions on the ICC could mean for international justice and how the court\'s supporters can respond.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/the-us-just-sanctioned-the-international-criminal-court-whats-next/'}, {'signal_id': 'ad1a2438dab4ecfa', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The war and the new energy narrative: How minerals redefine the Middle East’s strategic position <p>The Middle East crisis warrants diversification beyond energy exports into minerals, processing, manufacturing, and digital infrastructure partnerships.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="ht', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/energysource/the-war-and-the-new-energy-narrative-how-minerals-redefine-the-middle-easts-strategic-position/'}, {'signal_id': '1a2dc3c5325ef575', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in The Times on her new book, ‘The Undersea War’ <p>On October 9, Elisabeth Braw was mentioned in The Times in a book review of her recently released book, &#8216;The Undersea War.&#8217;</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-the-times-o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-the-times-on-her-new-book-the-undersea-war/'}, {'signal_id': '584de0f0a5759828', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Enabling NATO’s technological transformation <p>NATO faces persistent challenges in translating technological potential into operational capability. Recent analysis of NATO innovation efforts suggests that the limiting factor is often the ability of organizations and operators to', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/enabling-natos-technological-transformation/'}, {'signal_id': '17bcd601e818e2dd', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How the world fell out of love with French debt <p>French debt was supposed to be Europe’s “safe asset.” Not anymore.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/how-the-world-fell-out-of-love-with-french-debt/">How the world fell out of love with French d', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/how-the-world-fell-out-of-love-with-french-debt/'}, {'signal_id': '150d689e01f96d5c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Russia has rejected another Black Sea ceasefire. What next? <p>Russia’s latest ceasefire rejection leaves Black Sea security dependent on credible deterrence and increased allied support for Ukraine.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/turkeysource/russ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/turkeysource/russia-rejects-another-black-sea-ceasefire-with-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': 'a09c424ac0016e3c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Ukraine can help Europe counter Russia’s escalating shadow war <p>From Leipzig Airport to the Black Sea, Russia’s campaign of gray zone aggression against Europe has been escalating at an alarming rate in recent months. Ukraine's experience can help European leaders find the righ", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraine-can-help-europe-counter-russias-escalating-shadow-war/'}, {'signal_id': 'c48058e81be93f54', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Starving Ukrainians must travel ‘road of death’ to flee Russian occupation <p>A humanitarian catastrophe is unfolding in Russian-occupied southern Ukraine as the Kremlin authorities refuse to allow the evacuation of starving Ukrainian civilians trapped in front line city Oleshky,', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/starving-ukrainians-must-travel-road-of-death-to-flee-russian-occupation/'}, {'signal_id': 'db2e934045abc1b0', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': "Are yearlong deployments the Navy’s new normal? That's what officials are telling sailors' families in Japan, where two destroyers are slated for 12- and 14-month cruises.", 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/policy/2026/10/yearlong-deployments-navy-new-normal/416777/'}, {'signal_id': '2e8559f1c4dc5023', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Defense Business Brief: A little bit of MOSA; Netherlands-U.S. industry days, and more', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/business/2026/10/defense-business-brief-little-bit-mosa-netherlands-us-industry-days-and-more/416776/'}, {'signal_id': 'caaa65ffc30737b2', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Qatar looks to bolster its militar