signal_id': 'a537fec313fe7fd7', 'source': 'nk_news', 'text_snippet': 'Settling in Seoul: How a South Korean alternative school helped find my dream “Settling in Seoul” is an NK News series featuring interviews with and columns by North Korean defectors, most of whom left the DPRK within the last few years. Readers may submit their questions for def', 'url': 'https://www.nknews.org/2026/07/ask-a-north-korean-how-an-alternative-school-helped-me-find-my-dream/'}, {'signal_id': '59b12f8aa0eb6723', 'source': 'csis_korea', 'text_snippet': 'Iran can’t have nuclear weapons but North Korea can? There’s logic here. <p>There’s real logic beneath Trump’s split nuclear strategy. Iran and North Korea present very different nonproliferation problems.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://beyondparallel.csis.org/iran-cant-have-nu', 'url': 'https://beyondparallel.csis.org/iran-cant-have-nuclear-weapons-but-north-korea-can-theres-logic-here/'}, {'signal_id': '3eeb5573508c5d93', 'source': 'csis_korea', 'text_snippet': "After Iran: A Scenario for Renewed Trump-Kim Summitry <p>Why would North Korea's leader be interested in more summits with Trump? If Kim Jong-un is a revisionist in his outlook, he would look to capitalize on any available opportunity to advance the core goal of cementing his sta", 'url': 'https://beyondparallel.csis.org/after-iran-a-scenario-for-renewed-trump-kim-summitry/'}, {'signal_id': '9f89192d9402c2b9', 'source': 'csis_korea', 'text_snippet': 'North Korea As It Is: The Case for a Cold Peace <p>Dr. Victor Cha argues it\'s time to stop pretending the old framework can work and instead build a "cold peace" — a relationship short of normalization that manages the North Korean threat as it actually is.</p>\n<p>The post <a hre', 'url': 'https://beyondparallel.csis.org/north-korea-as-it-is-the-case-for-a-cold-peace/'}, {'signal_id': 'd32218443011fd74', 'source': 'csis_korea', 'text_snippet': 'Suspected Uranium Enrichment Building at Yongbyon Complete <p>Recent imagery shows